  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I was kinda surprised between 2 avatars with 45MB download size and 5MB download size, both have Medium Rank.\nBut why? My experience the unpack process of big avatars takes bit longer and it's also much longer to download fully. Such avatars with big pack size should not flagged as Medium, but more like Red flagged. It's possible it has big textures, causing avatar is bigger.\n\nIn my opinion, the big avatars (i mean big download pack) should give red mark. It's just not right to give red flag, its also kinda weird. We have people with slow internet, and imagine download many medium ranked with each 50 MB in size... oh that is just bad. You must wait much longer for everyone...\n\nSure it might not look heavy, but download time and storage is much bigger and takes more time to complete. And... it causes short lag spike when big avatar is downloaded and ready to activate.\n\nI hope small download size will more \"rewarded\" with better medium rank, ofc there are more reasons why even small avatars are red, due lights and many dynamic bones, for example.\n\nIf you do it for people with slow internet, they can set max rank until Medium, so too big avatars can \"skipped\" for them, and world is faster ready for them. The ranking system will have better meaning for everyone. :-)\n\nOr... add max download size to control it better? That is also good idea.",
